  "title": "New Kingdom of Egypt",
  "summary": "The New Kingdom (c. 1570–1069 BCE) followed the disunity of Egypt's Second Intermediate Period and is known as its age of empire. Thebes, on the site of modern Luxor, served as capital, with great temples and palaces at Karnak and Luxor and tombs in the Valley of the Kings. Every New Kingdom ruler added to the temple of Amun at Karnak. The era ended with the breakdown of central government.",
